# netsurf: a new block holding an iframe is built alone (patch 429)
# Generated 2026-11-09
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 428)
#
# "new element is not a plain block, list item or block of blocks" was
# r141's top decline (11). Logged in a scratch build, 6 of them were a
# <div> holding an <iframe> -- ad and embed slots inserted between blocks:
# cnnlite 2 ([DIV, IFRAME] inside), guardian 2, rte 2. The rest: youtube's
# <c3-icon> (an unknown element) in a flex box, google's <div> holding a
# <g-dropdown-menu>, claude's <div> of <div>s holding something else.
#
# html_rl_oc_tag (patch 364: images and form controls a new block may
# hold; the block built alone, the page laid out whole) admits iframe. A
# new frame box gets its record and its late load as in a full build
# (box_iframe, patch 244), as 378's appended and 407's inserted frames
# already do; no old frame box is freed. A new block that fails to build
# now also drops the frame records the build made
# (html_rl_frames_drop_new, patch 428) -- they pointed at its freed boxes
# (407's iframe leaves had the same gap).
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-09 13:14:16.277877468 +0000
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c	2026-11-09 13:33:07.205176796 +0000
@@ -6338,14 +6338,19 @@
